// TheatreDef: the Saltreach chart (DESIGN.md L735-751, L455, L1131-1146). Unit `data-theatre-acts`. Licensed CC BY 4.0.
// Generated from one layout script and committed as data; edit values here directly.
//
// Four regions of 12 nodes, opening one per act from the west. Every region runs the same logistics shape:
// its shipyard feeds two depots, the north one only through the region's chokepoint (the first sea node).
// Cutting the chokepoint cancels the north depot's convoys (the detour is over 1.5x) and reroutes the south
// depot's by the harbour (under 1.5x), so one raid drops Supply to about 40-45 and two cuts starve the region.
// Coves are leaves with no Combine traffic, so convoys never route through LANTERN's anchorages.
// Region 2 fields the Act 2 classes beside Act 1 hulls still in service (unit data-act2); region 3 fields the Act 3
// classes, its submarines among them, beside Act 1 and Act 2 hulls still in service (unit data-act3); region 4
// fields the Act 4 classes beside Act 2 and Act 3 hulls still in service, Act 3's boats among them (unit
// data-act4). Capitals and ace ships are never pooled hulls: they sail only in the groups an operation names.
// Sortie maps: X east, Z south, metres from the map centre. Every map carries the full marker vocabulary the
// operations name (spawn, enemy, enemy_2, objective, lane, exit, convoy_entry, convoy_exit, survivors, berth,
// landing, depot, radar); shore markers sit 0.35 to 0.5 shelf widths off their island's furthest shore, every
// other marker clear of all land and shelves.
// The sun table values are PLACEHOLDERS pending an owner decision (DESIGN.md L743).
